Subject: Justification for Cantor M2B Platform Preflight Forms

& [Claim] is narrow
  + [statement] implement strict effect-free platform-preflight records before authorizing any physical Win32 preflight
  + [confidence] is high

& [Support] is concrete
  + [dependency] exact generated ABI surface is already proven
  + [gap] no canonical record currently separates open failure, query failure, complete evidence, and disposition
  + [official_docs] define volume, final-path, file-identity, and remote-protocol query outputs
  + [existing_semantics] StrongFileIdentity and canonical volume-GUID path are already proven

& [WhyBeforeCalls] is governance critical
  + [reason] a probe that designs its record after observing the host can hide missing fields or normalize inconvenient failures
  + [result] the later physical probe must satisfy a fixed complete-or-fault contract

& [WhySumType] is honesty preserving
  + [reason] partial query output can be mistaken for complete admission
  + [result] open_fault and query_fault structurally cannot carry complete evidence

& [Counterarguments] are answered
  + [counterargument] call the APIs and print arbitrary JSON first
  + [answer] arbitrary output is not a stable semantic or proof contract
  + [counterargument] fold preflight directly into the scanner
  + [answer] platform eligibility and recursive topology correctness are separate gates
  + [counterargument] protocol zero is definitively local
  + [answer] it is a bounded policy inference and must be invalidated on contradictory target evidence

& [Invalidation] is explicit
  + [condition] source change, official semantic contradiction, inconsistent form, effect surface, failed test, stale evidence, or runtime overclaim
  + [response] stop and reprocess before physical continuation

& [Rollback] is direct
  + [module] remove platform_preflight_forms.rs
  + [export] remove the lib.rs module and re-export
  + [state] no migration exists
